From: TensorFold recipe <noreply@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] dsv41 lanes: a prompt with pictures resumes and keeps prompt states, keyed by the pictures' content

Rationale (issue #2 of this recipe): the prompt cache finds a kept state by the prompt's tokens, and every picture's positions hold the
same placeholder token, so a prompt with pictures was never looked up and never kept ("a kept state knows no images"): every turn of
a conversation that carries a picture in its history ran from 0 (about 90 s at 160K tokens in the report). Now the server gives such a
request a cache key of the same length, the pictures' positions replaced by ids made from a hash of the picture's payload (above every
vocabulary id: the same picture always makes the same ids, a different picture never does), and the history's length counted in the
expanded prompt; the host looks up and keeps by that key; the backend restores a state like any other and, resuming at its end, gives
the tower and the follower the rows only of the pictures the pass still embeds (a picture wholly before the cut is in the state;
its positions stay dead for Engram's n-grams). A request with pictures and no key (Request.cache_key empty) is refused by the cache as
before, so a server without the key can never match two different pictures. Applies after 0005 (the prefill interleave).

Switch: TF_DS_IMAGE_CACHE=0 (server) turns it off: no key, no history length, pictures resume and keep nothing as before. Unset = on.
Adds host tests (a picture's conversation resumes its state, another picture in the same positions does not, a request without a key
neither resumes nor keeps).

Written for this recipe; no code copied from other projects.
---
